  "analysis": "We have confirmed `__start` calls `doomgeneric_Create(0,0)` then loops `doomgeneric_Tick()` forever. `time` uses syscall 201. `gettimeofday` returns 0. I still need the full disassembly of syscall wrappers and the my_stdlib source. The output is often truncated because commands are batched. I'll run fewer commands per batch and save outputs to files for reliable viewing.",
  "plan": "Save my_stdlib.c to a numbered file and print focused ranges. Disassemble the syscall wrapper region and save it to a file, then print relevant portions. This should give exact syscall numbers and conventions.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "nl -ba /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.c > /tmp/my_stdlib_nl.txt; sed -n '1,120p' /tmp/my_stdlib_nl.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mips-linux-gnu-objdump -d --start-address=0x43d940 --stop-address=0x43dc90 /app/doomgeneric_mips > /tmp/syscalls_disasm.txt; sed -n '1,180p' /tmp/syscalls_disasm.txt\n",
      "duration": 1.0
